===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|ussher}}, {{m|enm|uscher}}, {{m|enm|usscher}}, from {{der|en|xno|usser}} and {{der|en|fro|ussier}}, {{m|fro|uissier||porter, doorman}} (compare {{cog|fr|huissier}}), from {{der|en|VL.||*ustiārius|doorkeeper}}, from {{der|en|la|ōstiārius}}, from {{m|la|ōstium||door}}. Akin to {{m|la|ōs||mouth}}. Probably a {{doublet|en|ostiary|huissier|nocap=1}}.

